      "sourceTextSha256": "f83d71df0b43c8566971f441586dfd50505e1dfc0d3fb4b59916c8d9f3712ed6",
      "text": "Day 10 · Transfer to Izabal and the Río Dulce, Guatemala’s most picturesque river, in a region of karst hills and caves, rivers, lakes and wetlands rich in birds and wildlife. A boat journey between the sheer walls of the river canyon, past hot springs and tropical jungle, leads to Livingston, reachable only by water: home of the Garifuna people, whose culture blends African, Caribbean and Indigenous roots, with palm trees, music and seafood; try tapado, a seafood soup cooked in coconut milk. Overnight at Hotel Villa Caribe. (B)",
